<title>INDIA: FORECAST - Indian rupee seen slipping to 36.59 a dlr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Indian rupee seen slipping to 36.59 a dlr.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian rupee is seen weakening by an average two percent to 36.59 against the dollar by July 31, according to a Reuters poll of leading banks and companies on Friday.</p>
<p>The rupee was quoted at 35.85 on Friday.</p>
<p>The average forecast showed the rupee at 36.04 by the end of next month and at 36.22 by the end of March.  </p>
<p>--</p>
